  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Now, domain of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br />For the range of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>∵</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>∴</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is the range<br />Also,&nbsp;<math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is an odd function<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> can be positive &amp; negative <math><mo>∀</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is many-one"
